1
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:07,695
Now I've taken weakness as my ally

2
00:00:07,696 --> 00:00:11,347
I can fly to the highest heights

3
00:00:11,347 --> 00:00:14,130
If I would just stop here

4
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:18,782
all I've lost would lose its luster

5
00:00:18,782 --> 00:00:22,304
If you were lost out somewhere

6
00:00:22,304 --> 00:00:25,912
at the same time my heart is shaken

7
00:00:25,913 --> 00:00:28,782
Id have no way to find you

8
00:00:28,782 --> 00:00:32,826
your kindness, or even your strength

9
00:00:32,826 --> 00:00:38,521
I know...

10
00:00:38,521 --> 00:00:40,391
It's time for the dawn!

11
00:00:40,478 --> 00:00:43,782
My peak performance

12
00:00:43,869 --> 00:00:47,826
I'll blow straight past in a blast, yeah

13
00:00:47,826 --> 00:00:50,608
You'll be left frozen with laughs

14
00:00:50,608 --> 00:00:55,043
The days of pain left in the past, let's hope

15
00:00:55,043 --> 00:00:57,869
As I make foes of the world

16
00:00:57,869 --> 00:01:02,304
Im bracing myself upon shaking legs, yeah

17
00:01:02,304 --> 00:01:05,043
Just keep me going for a few more steps

18
00:01:05,043 --> 00:01:09,912
Now, this is the comeback, the time to awaken is now

19
00:01:19,521 --> 00:01:24,478
Now, this is the comeback, the time to awaken is now

20
00:01:41,043 --> 00:01:42,303
Taste good?

21
00:01:43,174 --> 00:01:45,304
Tastes so good!

22
00:01:45,304 --> 00:01:49,130
Hey, guys!
I found a shaved ice stall over there!

23
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:50,782
Shaved ice!

24
00:01:50,782 --> 00:01:53,608
I wanna try shaved ice, too!

25
00:01:54,217 --> 00:01:57,130
Let's go, O-Nami-chan!

26
00:01:57,130 --> 00:01:58,304
Mm-hmm!

27
00:01:58,347 --> 00:02:00,999
O-Nami-chan, hurry, hurry!
bos

28
00:02:01,739 --> 00:02:04,086
There're so many flavors!

29
00:02:04,086 --> 00:02:06,608
I can't decide!

30
00:02:06,608 --> 00:02:09,999
I wanna try the oshiruko flavor!

31
00:02:19,174 --> 00:02:21,174
Annoying scum!

32
00:02:28,043 --> 00:02:29,825
I see no end to this!

33
00:02:32,782 --> 00:02:35,347
Momonosuke-kun!
I will lend you aid!

34
00:02:37,869 --> 00:02:38,739
You will not!

35
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:43,825
But why?!
Why will you not allow me to fight?!

36
00:02:43,826 --> 00:02:46,478
You mustn't!
You must not lay your hand upon him...!

37
00:02:46,869 --> 00:02:48,217
Yamato!

38
00:03:00,739 --> 00:03:05,435
Just bring Straw Hat Luffy
to me already, dammit!

39
00:03:12,652 --> 00:03:15,304
Ninja Art: Scrolling Technique!

40
00:03:22,652 --> 00:03:23,913
Fire Escape!

41
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:33,564
Burn to ash...

42
00:03:35,435 --> 00:03:37,739
Navy filth!

43
00:03:43,608 --> 00:03:44,956
Just kidding!

44
00:03:49,391 --> 00:03:50,782
Firebreak Forest!

45
00:03:52,435 --> 00:03:56,043
How the hell could I possibly serve
as a Navy Admiral...

46
00:03:56,086 --> 00:03:59,651
...with such an obvious weakness?!

47
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:13,564
Water's important for
nature and humans...

48
00:04:13,565 --> 00:04:14,565
Ya know?

49
00:04:15,608 --> 00:04:17,043
Unhand me!

50
00:04:27,652 --> 00:04:29,565
Raizo!

51
00:04:29,608 --> 00:04:32,391
Foul beast! Cut as we might,
they keep growing back!

52
00:04:32,391 --> 00:04:34,174
Raizo-san!

53
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:43,000
Does he-gara have no weakness?!

54
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,261
Do we really gotta cut
all o' them?!

55
00:04:46,957 --> 00:04:47,609
Dog!

56
00:04:50,043 --> 00:04:51,129
Blast-

57
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:00,173
Momonosuke-kun...

58
00:05:00,739 --> 00:05:01,913
Why?

59
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:10,217
Stairs?

60
00:05:16,043 --> 00:05:16,695
Oh?

61
00:05:17,043 --> 00:05:18,999
How did you sniff us out here?

62
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,391
You weren't with the others.
Of course I'd find that suspicious.

63
00:05:22,391 --> 00:05:24,348
Don't talk about me like
I'm some hyena.

64
00:05:26,086 --> 00:05:28,390
Do watch your step.

65
00:05:28,391 --> 00:05:29,739
'Tis moldy.

66
00:05:31,782 --> 00:05:35,912
I told neither Kaido
nor Orochi of this route...

67
00:05:35,913 --> 00:05:39,739
But as the All-Star Jack is a Fishman,

68
00:05:39,739 --> 00:05:43,565
they found the Poneglyph in no time.

69
00:05:43,565 --> 00:05:46,738
How would being
a Fishman help find it?

70
00:05:46,739 --> 00:05:48,174
Best to see for oneself.

71
00:05:49,435 --> 00:05:52,000
Just how deep are we going?

72
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,130
Well...

73
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:56,695
Centuries into the past.

74
00:06:02,043 --> 00:06:03,695
Say, Tengu-san...

75
00:06:03,696 --> 00:06:06,696
What might be
the source of this dim light?

76
00:06:09,478 --> 00:06:12,435
A block of glass is installed there.

77
00:06:12,435 --> 00:06:14,478
Peer through it,
if you so wish.

78
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,087
We have reached the ocean floor.

79
00:06:21,782 --> 00:06:22,912
Room.

80
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:26,217
Eh?

81
00:06:26,608 --> 00:06:27,565
Now that's unfair!

82
00:06:28,435 --> 00:06:29,391
See anything?

83
00:06:39,696 --> 00:06:41,652
The Land of Wano...
on the seafloor?!

84
00:06:45,521 --> 00:06:49,738
That is the Land of Wano,
eight hundred years ago.

85
00:06:49,739 --> 00:06:51,304
Or rather, what once was.

86
00:06:56,826 --> 00:07:00,347
"Eight hundred years ago"?
What do you mean by that?

87
00:07:00,696 --> 00:07:02,608
'Tis precisely as I say.

88
00:07:02,608 --> 00:07:06,695
But I know not what transpired
to have caused what you see.

89
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:14,478
And as that is not seawater in which it lies,
it is relatively well-preserved.

90
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,217
This is what I know:4

91
00:07:17,217 --> 00:07:21,434
The Land of Wano was once located
at a base of a great mountain named Fujiyama.

92
00:07:22,043 --> 00:07:24,956
At one point walls were built,
enclosing the island,

93
00:07:24,957 --> 00:07:27,043
causing rainwater to accumulate over time.

94
00:07:27,521 --> 00:07:30,260
People abandoned these
now-uninhabitable towns,

95
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:35,390
moved up the mountain,
and founded a new country.

96
00:07:38,217 --> 00:07:40,130
And that's the current Land of Wano?

97
00:07:40,652 --> 00:07:41,956
Indeed.

98
00:07:47,869 --> 00:07:49,695
And here we are!

99
00:08:06,826 --> 00:08:08,521
A Road Poneglyph...

100
00:08:09,652 --> 00:08:12,000
This makes three,
I do believe...

101
00:08:12,435 --> 00:08:15,695
If we find the one remaining,
we can reach Laugh Tale.

102
00:08:17,826 --> 00:08:18,565
We tread upon...

103
00:08:18,565 --> 00:08:22,478
...the high ground in a cave
at the foot of Fujiyama.

104
00:08:25,696 --> 00:08:27,826
And what is more, so they say...

105
00:08:28,217 --> 00:08:31,434
...the Ancient Weapon Pluton
lies deeper still!

106
00:08:31,826 --> 00:08:32,391
What?

107
00:08:33,174 --> 00:08:38,565
I have never seen it myself,
not that I could even show it to you now.

108
00:08:38,565 --> 00:08:43,130
To retrieve it requires
dismantling of the walls!

109
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:46,695
In other words, to "open the borders" would mean
destroying the defensive walls,

110
00:08:46,696 --> 00:08:50,087
and unleashing the Ancient Weapon!

111
00:08:57,260 --> 00:08:59,912
Opening the borders
means unleashing the weapon?

112
00:08:59,913 --> 00:09:03,522
Why would Kozuki Oden
have wanted to do such a thing?

113
00:09:06,608 --> 00:09:09,782
This is the sum of what has been
handed down within the Shogunate.

114
00:09:10,435 --> 00:09:15,000
I know nothing of what
Oden discovered abroad...

115
00:09:22,347 --> 00:09:23,912
Yummy!

116
00:09:24,696 --> 00:09:27,261
Yum, mmm!

117
00:09:29,347 --> 00:09:33,217
Hey, Bepo!
There was a shaved ice stall!

118
00:09:33,217 --> 00:09:35,913
What?! Shaved ice?!
Where?! Where?!

119
00:09:49,869 --> 00:09:51,695
Leave this place at once!

120
00:09:51,696 --> 00:09:53,217
Momonosuke-sama!

121
00:09:55,391 --> 00:09:59,565
Mere humans're no match
for Mother Nature!

122
00:09:59,565 --> 00:10:01,260
Don't ya get it?

123
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:04,651
If Kaido were here, I wouldn't be!

124
00:10:05,826 --> 00:10:09,130
Hate to admit it,
but Kaido's sheer dominance...

125
00:10:09,130 --> 00:10:12,913
...kept this country's enemies at bay!

126
00:10:14,478 --> 00:10:18,174
If you can understand that much,
you'll bring Straw Hat Luffy to me!

127
00:10:18,521 --> 00:10:22,651
Soon as I lop off his head,
I'm outta here!

128
00:10:24,391 --> 00:10:27,565
Momonosuke-kun!
Let us turn to Luffy and his crew for aid!

129
00:10:27,565 --> 00:10:29,347
They will not lose to this fool!

130
00:10:34,478 --> 00:10:36,130
We cannot do that!

131
00:10:36,739 --> 00:10:37,956
Eh?

132
00:10:37,957 --> 00:10:41,130
And we will not accept aid from you, either!
Do not aid us!

133
00:10:41,608 --> 00:10:47,217
You were imprisoned within Onigashima for so long,
and now you can finally be free!

134
00:10:48,130 --> 00:10:50,304
And so, I will give you
a proper send-off!

135
00:10:50,304 --> 00:10:54,434
For too long have I been dependent upon
Luffy, Zoro, and their allies!

136
00:10:54,957 --> 00:10:58,957
If those of us that remain in this country
cannot drive out our enemies...

137
00:11:01,130 --> 00:11:03,521
If we rely on those
who will be departing...

138
00:11:04,304 --> 00:11:06,434
We will have proven our inability...

139
00:11:06,435 --> 00:11:09,130
...to defend our land in the future!

140
00:11:11,174 --> 00:11:12,782
Momonosuke-kun...

141
00:11:12,782 --> 00:11:16,086
Begone, foul creature of wood!

142
00:11:21,217 --> 00:11:24,174
Why?! Why can I not bring it forth?!

143
00:11:25,913 --> 00:11:29,478
Oh, wow...
He's kinda like a kid.

144
00:11:29,478 --> 00:11:32,435
Who knew there was
such a worthless dragon?

145
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:41,782
Get out!

146
00:11:52,478 --> 00:11:54,304
I did it!

147
00:11:56,304 --> 00:11:58,086
Momonosuke-sama!

148
00:11:58,086 --> 00:12:00,651
Amazing, 'tis practically as Kaido's...!

149
00:12:00,869 --> 00:12:02,912
Get out!

150
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,913
Get out, and begone from our land!

151
00:12:06,782 --> 00:12:08,260
Dammit...!

152
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:10,304
Now hold on, dumbass!

153
00:12:13,174 --> 00:12:17,130
Incredible! He has mastered
his dragon form!

154
00:12:17,696 --> 00:12:20,739
Alas, his aim is not the most steady...

155
00:12:51,608 --> 00:12:53,043
Oopsie daisy...

156
00:12:53,043 --> 00:12:55,782
Tryin' to burn down
the whole damn village, huh...

157
00:12:55,782 --> 00:12:59,217
You want a fight,
I'll give ya a fight...

158
00:12:59,217 --> 00:13:02,043
Frickin' Kaido wannabe...

159
00:13:02,043 --> 00:13:05,390
I'm gonna skewer ya,
mouth to tail!

160
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,739
Can't move...

161
00:13:22,739 --> 00:13:25,130
Conqueror's Haki?!

162
00:13:25,217 --> 00:13:26,695
Whose the hell is it?!

163
00:13:29,826 --> 00:13:31,912
Don't tell me...

164
00:13:32,521 --> 00:13:34,869
The Red-Hair Pirates?!

165
00:13:35,435 --> 00:13:37,521
Is that who's there?!

166
00:13:40,304 --> 00:13:41,651
C'mon, Boss!

167
00:13:41,652 --> 00:13:43,739
Ya can't just whip out your Haki like that!

168
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:46,174
It's too hard on our new crewmates!

169
00:13:47,217 --> 00:13:50,652
I won't tell you it's unfair, Navy dog...

170
00:13:51,478 --> 00:13:56,043
But going after these exhausted "sprouts"
just after they changed pirate history...

171
00:13:56,043 --> 00:13:58,651
...is a bit tasteless, don't you think?

172
00:14:00,435 --> 00:14:04,348
The new era really
scaring you that much?

173
00:14:07,043 --> 00:14:10,129
I'm not here to fight your bunch!

174
00:14:10,130 --> 00:14:11,652
Not yet, anyway!

175
00:14:12,565 --> 00:14:14,173
All right, already!

176
00:14:16,608 --> 00:14:18,434
Marvelous!

177
00:14:18,435 --> 00:14:21,478
You did it, Momonosuke-kun!
You drove him out!

178
00:14:21,478 --> 00:14:24,000
You defended Wano!

179
00:14:25,217 --> 00:14:27,478
I defended Wano?

180
00:14:34,174 --> 00:14:36,521
I defended my country?

181
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,652
You are incredible, Momonosuke-kun!

182
00:14:44,696 --> 00:14:46,174
There he goes!

183
00:14:46,174 --> 00:14:48,391
Good on ya, Momo!

184
00:14:48,739 --> 00:14:50,609
Guess we don't get a turn.

185
00:14:53,869 --> 00:14:57,173
Hell of a Haki that was, though...

186
00:14:57,174 --> 00:15:00,000
Yeah... What was that?

187
00:15:05,826 --> 00:15:08,130
Kinda made me think of
a familiar face...!

188
00:15:16,608 --> 00:15:17,999
Raizo!

189
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,043
Shinobu-san!
You must live!

190
00:15:22,869 --> 00:15:26,739
I can scarcely believe
Raizo and Shinobu wasted away like this...

191
00:15:26,739 --> 00:15:28,522
Most terrifying sorcery, it is.

192
00:15:28,957 --> 00:15:32,826
Frustrating as it is,
he spoke the truth.

193
00:15:33,217 --> 00:15:38,608
Kaido served as a deterrent
against enemies of this nation...

194
00:15:38,608 --> 00:15:40,782
Tis my shame to bear!

195
00:15:40,782 --> 00:15:41,999
My apologies!

196
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,739
I was in Kuri,
and as a result knew nothing of this!

197
00:15:45,739 --> 00:15:49,913
Ain't yer fault,
wasn't much harm done besides.

198
00:15:49,913 --> 00:15:52,782
An' it's all thanks ta
Momonosuke-sama's huge hand in it!

199
00:15:52,782 --> 00:15:53,956
So don'cha worry.

200
00:15:56,086 --> 00:15:59,869
By the way,
how's O-Tsuru-san these days?

201
00:15:59,869 --> 00:16:02,912
Well... Okobore Town
caught fire,

202
00:16:02,913 --> 00:16:07,130
and she suffered horrible burns,
yet she survived...

203
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:10,217
Oh, O-Tsuru-san!

204
00:16:10,217 --> 00:16:11,304
Yes?

205
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:13,477
I heard Kin-san came back!

206
00:16:13,478 --> 00:16:17,174
Yes, he has.
He already returned to the capital, though.

207
00:16:17,174 --> 00:16:21,043
You're from the capital, too.
You ought to go back for him!

208
00:16:21,043 --> 00:16:22,434
Aye.

209
00:16:22,435 --> 00:16:25,608
I would much like to be with him, too...

210
00:16:28,608 --> 00:16:33,304
My, my... Even twenty years later,
Tsuru has retained her beauty...

211
00:16:33,304 --> 00:16:37,738
Hey! Dogs like cheese,
but not that much cheese!

212
00:16:37,739 --> 00:16:40,130
Prrmeow meowmeow!

213
00:16:41,696 --> 00:16:44,174
How wonderful, Kin-sama!

214
00:16:49,652 --> 00:16:51,782
What is the matter, Raizo?!

215
00:16:51,782 --> 00:16:53,739
Do you want something?

216
00:16:53,739 --> 00:16:55,652
I want...

217
00:16:55,652 --> 00:16:56,652
What is it?

218
00:16:58,608 --> 00:17:01,217
to be popular, too.

219
00:17:01,217 --> 00:17:04,739
You-gara need to
recuperate first, Raizo!

220
00:17:07,043 --> 00:17:09,129
This is big monkeyin' news!

221
00:17:13,435 --> 00:17:14,913
Found you!

222
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:20,695
Want shome oden?

223
00:17:20,696 --> 00:17:25,565
Duke Inuarashi and Governor Nekomamushi
are howlin' for you!

224
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,652
There you are, Carrot.

225
00:17:31,652 --> 00:17:34,304
What's up?
You rang,

226
00:17:34,304 --> 00:17:37,217
Duke? Governor Nekomamushi?

227
00:17:37,217 --> 00:17:39,217
We was waitin' for ya.

228
00:17:56,260 --> 00:18:00,521
We were thinking of having you-gara succeed us
as ruler of the Mokomo Dukedom.

229
00:18:02,347 --> 00:18:03,782
Ruler?!

230
00:18:03,869 --> 00:18:05,347
Yaaaay!

231
00:18:05,347 --> 00:18:06,434
'Kay, sure!

232
00:18:13,608 --> 00:18:16,738
Whaaaa?!

233
00:18:16,739 --> 00:18:18,826
The ruler?!

234
00:18:18,826 --> 00:18:22,130
I dun wanna!
There's no way I can handle that!

235
00:18:22,130 --> 00:18:23,782
www
Thing is...

236
00:18:23,782 --> 00:18:29,130
...the cat and I have decided to stay here in Wano,
and as samurai of the Kozuki Clan,

237
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:32,478
we will protect Momonosuke-sama.

238
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:37,304
Prrrmeow meowmeow!

239
00:18:37,304 --> 00:18:42,347
You-gara went abroad with Luffy's crew,
somethin' few've done,

240
00:18:42,869 --> 00:18:46,739
so we's sure ya got what it takes
t'lead the next generation.

241
00:18:46,739 --> 00:18:48,478
Wait, hold on!

242
00:18:48,478 --> 00:18:51,652
There're so many others
that're stronger than me, though!

243
00:18:51,652 --> 00:18:53,087
That goes without saying!

244
00:18:54,391 --> 00:18:57,478
To guard the country
is our job!

245
00:18:57,913 --> 00:19:01,826
I'll support you, too. 11
This is what the Duke and the Governor decided.

246
00:19:10,217 --> 00:19:14,174
Carrot! Most of all of us, you-teia carry...

247
00:19:14,174 --> 00:19:16,260
...Pedro's will in your heart.

248
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,174
Pedro...

249
00:19:22,174 --> 00:19:24,130
The rest's up to yous.

250
00:19:24,130 --> 00:19:27,869
Zou's now in
you-gara youngsters' hands!

251
00:19:31,217 --> 00:19:33,130
You speak the truth...?

252
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:35,478
You are our grandfather?

253
00:19:35,478 --> 00:19:37,087
Mm.

254
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,261
am Oden's father.

255
00:19:43,304 --> 00:19:46,564
So you really were alive!

256
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,478
I am sorry...

257
00:19:48,478 --> 00:19:51,260
I could not bear to
show my face to you two.

258
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:53,738
I could not save Oden...

259
00:19:54,347 --> 00:19:59,260
...much less could I save our country.

260
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:01,956
For that, I am sorry...
So sorry...

261
00:20:01,957 --> 00:20:04,260
How I longed to see you!

262
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:05,869
As did !!

263
00:20:05,869 --> 00:20:07,608
Thank you.

264
00:20:08,478 --> 00:20:13,043
You are the very image of
Oden himself, Momonosuke!

265
00:20:13,043 --> 00:20:14,608
Grandfather!

266
00:20:15,304 --> 00:20:17,695
For us, having lost our parents,

267
00:20:18,217 --> 00:20:21,434
simply knowing we have
living relatives gives us great courage!

268
00:20:21,435 --> 00:20:23,782
I feel the same!

269
00:20:23,782 --> 00:20:27,130
So please, do not apologize!

270
00:20:36,086 --> 00:20:38,173
I was astonished!

271
00:20:38,652 --> 00:20:40,782
So he was Sukiyaki-sama!

272
00:20:40,869 --> 00:20:43,739
Not once did
the thought cross my mind!

273
00:20:43,739 --> 00:20:47,260
My heart leapt into my throat!

274
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:49,825
I am ever grateful
that he yet lives!

275
00:20:53,217 --> 00:20:56,869
I knew you lot would
certainly take notice...

276
00:20:56,869 --> 00:21:00,739
Who would wear a tengu mask
when there is no festival?

277
00:21:00,739 --> 00:21:03,652
We did not think you
a mere swordsmith.

278
00:21:03,957 --> 00:21:07,608
We felt it would be rude
to draw attention to the fact...

279
00:21:07,608 --> 00:21:09,434
Would you agree, Kin-sama?

280
00:21:11,782 --> 00:21:13,304
Indeed so!

281
00:21:14,391 --> 00:21:17,174
I regret to have had you
treat the issue so...

282
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:24,391
can impart to you our land's history,
but seeing as I am but a doddering old man,

283
00:21:24,391 --> 00:21:26,826
that is the extent of
what I am able to offer.

284
00:21:26,826 --> 00:21:31,695
I beg of you, do not tell our subjects of me.
Let me live out the rest of my days in peace.

285
00:21:32,130 --> 00:21:35,695
From this point onward,
the new era is yours to shape.

286
00:21:35,739 --> 00:21:39,609
Just the fact that you are alive
gives us strength!

287
00:21:48,478 --> 00:21:52,130
Say whadaa?!
Pluton's in this country?!

288
00:21:52,130 --> 00:21:55,478
Yes. I didn't get to see it, however...

289
00:21:55,478 --> 00:21:57,347
But it's here, for certain!

290
00:21:57,347 --> 00:22:00,173
That thing really exists, huh?

291
00:22:02,739 --> 00:22:05,304
Ain't that the thing Franky
had the blueprints to 'n burned 'em?

292
00:22:05,304 --> 00:22:06,477
That's right.

293
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,739
An Ancient Weapon,
bearing the name of a god:

294
00:22:09,739 --> 00:22:10,739
Pluton.

295
00:22:11,174 --> 00:22:13,695
Do you want it for yourself, Luffy?

296
00:22:13,696 --> 00:22:14,913
Nah, I dun need it.

297
00:22:15,347 --> 00:22:16,608
Thought not

298
00:22:17,174 --> 00:22:20,869
Yet, Oden attempted to unleash it.

299
00:22:21,435 --> 00:22:22,521
Why, I wonder?

300
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,348
What? What?
The bad guys!!

301
00:22:27,043 --> 00:22:28,173
What was that?

302
00:22:28,174 --> 00:22:30,304
Are you likening mature women...

303
00:22:30,304 --> 00:22:32,651
...to devastating weapons?

304
00:22:32,652 --> 00:22:34,782
Who the hellre you
s'posed to be?!

305
00:22:34,782 --> 00:22:38,130
Who am I, you ask?
Do you not recognize me?

306
00:22:38,130 --> 00:22:42,043
A minor incident may have
caused a little emaciation....

307
00:22:42,043 --> 00:22:44,912
...but 'tis I, Shinobu!

308
00:22:44,913 --> 00:22:47,261
Whaaaa?!

309
00:22:47,304 --> 00:22:49,564
That little bit of
emaciation did wonders!

310
00:22:49,565 --> 00:22:53,086
You look so incredible,
I've lost my backbone!

311
00:22:53,086 --> 00:22:56,216
Though I'm all bones to begin with!

312
00:22:59,043 --> 00:23:00,347
Big Bro, Big Bro!

313
00:23:01,782 --> 00:23:05,043
Shinobu-chan took me in
as her apprentice!

314
00:23:05,435 --> 00:23:07,826
I'mma get stronger
so's the next time we meet,

315
00:23:07,826 --> 00:23:10,260
I want ya to lemme join yer crew!

316
00:23:10,260 --> 00:23:12,608
If ya can use
ninja arts by then,

317
00:23:12,608 --> 00:23:13,651
you got it!

318
00:23:15,521 --> 00:23:17,043
Awwright!

319
00:23:17,043 --> 00:23:20,651
I'm gonna put in hard work 'n
become a bewitchin' ninja lady!

320
00:23:20,652 --> 00:23:21,869
Nin, nin!

321
00:23:21,869 --> 00:23:24,739
Oooh, you're such a cutie, O-Tama!

322
00:23:26,043 --> 00:23:28,782
You're the bestest!

323
00:23:31,521 --> 00:23:35,478
I can't believe it...
Pluton's in Wano?

324
00:23:35,869 --> 00:23:37,912
First Poseidon, and now this...

325
00:23:37,913 --> 00:23:43,261
I know someone who'll be
thrilled to hear about this!

326
00:23:59,608 --> 00:24:00,825
Shogun!

327
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:03,217
There you are!

328
00:24:05,565 --> 00:24:09,043
The regions have submitted their
individual reconstruction plans.

329
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:10,869
Let us see...

330
00:24:12,913 --> 00:24:15,869
That is the funding estimate.

331
00:24:15,869 --> 00:24:17,565
Mmm. Good work.

332
00:24:18,217 --> 00:24:19,521
Shogun!

333
00:24:19,869 --> 00:24:24,608
Proposals to repurpose
the weapon factory sites have come in.

334
00:24:24,608 --> 00:24:26,173
Mmm... Let us go, then.

335
00:24:31,957 --> 00:24:36,217
Shogun! I humbly request
your opinion on the reservoir later.

336
00:24:36,565 --> 00:24:40,565
We must talk about the
all-region meeting with the Daimyos!

337
00:24:40,565 --> 00:24:41,651
Mmm.

338
00:24:43,174 --> 00:24:44,826
Shogun!

339
00:24:47,043 --> 00:24:47,651
Mmm.

340
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:57,391
Hey, Zoro!

341
00:24:57,391 --> 00:25:00,347
Might you teach me some
of your sword tech...

342
00:25:00,347 --> 00:25:02,564
...niques...

343
00:25:04,478 --> 00:25:06,478
Luffy? Zoro?

344
00:25:12,435 --> 00:25:14,826
O-Nami! Usopp!

345
00:25:14,869 --> 00:25:16,782
Sanji!

346
00:25:16,869 --> 00:25:18,521
Chopperemon!

347
00:25:18,913 --> 00:25:20,869
Robin! Franky!

348
00:25:20,869 --> 00:25:23,565
Bonekichi! Jinbe!

349
00:25:23,913 --> 00:25:25,391
Yamato!

350
00:25:26,217 --> 00:25:28,130
Where is everyone?!

351
00:25:29,391 --> 00:25:30,826
Anyone?!

352
00:25:34,086 --> 00:25:36,651
Hiyori! Have you seen
Luffy and the others?!

353
00:25:37,304 --> 00:25:40,434
They have departed after
bidding their farewells to everyone...

354
00:25:41,739 --> 00:25:43,391
I'm so sad!

355
00:25:46,608 --> 00:25:48,434
"Bidding their farewells"?

356
00:25:48,435 --> 00:25:50,782
Yet they said
nothing of this to me...

357
00:25:52,739 --> 00:25:54,782
Momonosuke-sama!

358
00:25:54,782 --> 00:25:58,347
Ki-Kin'emon!
Luffy and his crew have...

359
00:25:58,347 --> 00:26:00,130
I have just learned
of this as well!

360
00:26:00,174 --> 00:26:02,695
What?! You, too, Kin'emon?!

361
00:26:02,696 --> 00:26:06,913
I inquired, and Denjiro and the others
have already bade them farewell!

362
00:26:06,913 --> 00:26:10,826
Why did they not
say anything to us!!

363
00:26:23,347 --> 00:26:26,304
Pick another date, Straw Hatter!

364
00:26:27,435 --> 00:26:28,608
Why the hell do I gotta?!

365
00:26:28,608 --> 00:26:30,521
Cause it's weird!

366
00:26:30,521 --> 00:26:33,521
Settin' sail together, I mean!

367
00:26:33,521 --> 00:26:37,086
The alliance is done!
We're enemies now.

368
00:26:37,086 --> 00:26:40,564
My crew decided we'd set off today!

369
00:26:40,565 --> 00:26:41,651
Same here!

370
00:26:41,957 --> 00:26:45,260
You change first, Trafalgar!

371
00:26:45,260 --> 00:26:48,477
How about I not,
and you take your own advice?

372
00:26:48,478 --> 00:26:50,348
I ain't changin', neither!

373
00:26:50,739 --> 00:26:52,869
This is ridiculous...

374
00:26:52,869 --> 00:26:55,565
It's not like we all tried
to pick the same day...

375
00:26:55,565 --> 00:26:57,478
So we're pickin'
separate directions!

376
00:26:57,478 --> 00:27:00,739
The Log Pose locked on
to three directions...

377
00:27:00,739 --> 00:27:03,435
Northeast, east, and southeast!

378
00:27:03,869 --> 00:27:05,043
Choose.

379
00:27:05,043 --> 00:27:06,651
The middle one!

380
00:27:08,260 --> 00:27:10,043
I'm set, then...

381
00:27:11,174 --> 00:27:14,000
BeHeading northeast
will get you the farthest ahead.

382
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:16,347
Maybe try using your brains once in a while?

383
00:27:16,347 --> 00:27:17,217
Morons.

384
00:27:19,260 --> 00:27:20,782
"The middle one"?

385
00:27:21,957 --> 00:27:22,870
What are you, kids?

386
00:27:24,304 --> 00:27:26,304
That settles my destination.

387
00:27:26,304 --> 00:27:29,477
You two can figure out
the rest on your own, yeah?

388
00:27:29,478 --> 00:27:31,695
Straw Hat, pick one!

389
00:27:31,739 --> 00:27:34,260
One of 'em says "East"

390
00:27:34,260 --> 00:27:35,956
This'n!

391
00:27:39,608 --> 00:27:40,825
got "East"!

392
00:27:42,347 --> 00:27:44,260
I picked the loser!

393
00:27:44,260 --> 00:27:46,260
Sorry, guys!

394
00:27:47,826 --> 00:27:49,782
There's danger no matter
which way, dammit!

395
00:27:49,782 --> 00:27:53,260
Literally nobody cares!
Just help with the cargo, Luffy!

396
00:27:53,260 --> 00:27:57,260
I'm an Emperor of the Sea,
but I lost the raffle!

397
00:27:58,739 --> 00:28:00,000
Cry more,
why don'cha?!

398
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,304
But...

399
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:04,130
...when it comes to Emperors,
the one who really makes me mad...

400
00:28:04,130 --> 00:28:05,782
...is this guy!

401
00:28:08,043 --> 00:28:10,129
Buggy the Genius Jester!

402
00:28:10,130 --> 00:28:13,087
Hwuuuuh?!
The heck's up with this?!

403
00:28:20,739 --> 00:28:21,129
CROSS

404
00:28:25,130 --> 00:28:26,826
TRUSS
GUILD

405
00:28:26,826 --> 00:28:29,478
Those're Crocodile and
Hawkeye, ain't they?!

406
00:28:30,260 --> 00:28:32,434
Why're they showin' up like
they're under Buggy?!

407
00:28:32,435 --> 00:28:36,608
Nah, there's no way
Hawkeye'd work for him...

408
00:28:38,565 --> 00:28:42,565
If these two men are actually
under his command,

409
00:28:42,565 --> 00:28:45,260
then he's definitely earned the right
to be called an Emperor.

410
00:28:45,260 --> 00:28:48,564
But he's a total dumbass!
What the hell happened?

411
00:28:48,565 --> 00:28:52,434
Seems like this company
called Cross Guild...

412
00:28:52,435 --> 00:28:55,913
...started putting bounties on marines.

413
00:28:55,957 --> 00:28:58,391
The Navy were the hunters this whole time,

414
00:28:58,391 --> 00:29:02,304
...but now they gotta worry about
being hunted by civilians.

415
00:29:02,304 --> 00:29:05,651
While we were holed up
in this isolated country,

416
00:29:06,174 --> 00:29:09,391
the world's changed a ton.

417
00:29:11,826 --> 00:29:14,434
No complaints about
our directions, yeah?

418
00:29:14,435 --> 00:29:18,695
Soon as we sail outta here,
it's back to bein' a free-for-all!

419
00:29:25,086 --> 00:29:28,608
What's this, Trafalgar?

420
00:29:28,608 --> 00:29:30,695
Copy of a Road Poneglyph.

421
00:29:31,043 --> 00:29:33,303
You've earned your right to it,
same as us.

422
00:29:33,957 --> 00:29:36,000
Cheating takes all the fun out of it...

423
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:39,347
So Kaido did have one, as I thought...

424
00:29:39,347 --> 00:29:42,869
Same kinda thing that we got from
one of Big Mom's generals?

425
00:29:44,696 --> 00:29:48,739
We'd better get serious about this too, Kid!

426
00:29:48,739 --> 00:29:52,260
If we wanna be in the running
for the One Piece...

427
00:29:52,260 --> 00:29:55,912
We need to find
"the Man with the Burn Scar", right?

428
00:29:55,913 --> 00:29:57,783
But we hardly got any leads...

429
00:29:58,957 --> 00:30:00,565
"Burn Scar"?

430
00:30:00,565 --> 00:30:01,695
What's that about?

431
00:30:06,608 --> 00:30:08,217
You don't know, huh?!

432
00:30:09,130 --> 00:30:11,478
Works out for us, then!

433
00:30:12,826 --> 00:30:14,304
What's that?!
Spit it out!

434
00:30:14,304 --> 00:30:18,086
Hey, Yamato!

435
00:30:18,086 --> 00:30:20,216
Where are you?!

436
00:30:20,217 --> 00:30:22,521
Yamato!

437
00:30:22,521 --> 00:30:24,651
Are you not here, either?!

438
00:30:24,652 --> 00:30:26,826
Yamato!

439
00:30:27,782 --> 00:30:29,260
Momonosuke-kun!

440
00:30:29,304 --> 00:30:31,390
I am over here!

441
00:30:31,435 --> 00:30:32,869
Where, though?

442
00:30:34,260 --> 00:30:36,260
Your usual spot on the roof, I take it?

443
00:30:37,391 --> 00:30:40,174
Right, then!
I have decided!

444
00:30:49,565 --> 00:30:52,782
Let us go to where
Luffy and his crew are!

445
00:30:55,869 --> 00:30:57,217
1...

446
00:30:57,217 --> 00:30:59,826
...Shall live as Kozuki Oden did!

447
00:31:33,608 --> 00:31:36,260
"Time's up'

448
00:31:37,565 --> 00:31:41,087
Someone said again, with a laugh

449
00:31:41,521 --> 00:31:46,087
Fine then, hide-and-seek playtime...

450
00:31:46,652 --> 00:31:47,739
...is over

451
00:31:49,521 --> 00:31:52,869
Let's go, come on (We can see it soon)

452
00:31:53,043 --> 00:31:56,782
Let your heart beat out

453
00:31:57,782 --> 00:32:01,043
and things will change (We can see it soon)

454
00:32:01,304 --> 00:32:05,260
Grow strong, you have time

455
00:32:05,435 --> 00:32:06,218
Raise up that dream

456
00:32:06,478 --> 00:32:13,217
The overflowing loneliness can't sustain me alone

457
00:32:13,391 --> 00:32:17,348
We were so free in our younger days

458
00:32:17,478 --> 00:32:20,739
What a dumb dream

459
00:32:20,826 --> 00:32:22,000
...to live

460
00:32:22,043 --> 00:32:25,869
Shining a light on uncharted ways

461
00:32:25,957 --> 00:32:30,001
Get on our feet and try

462
00:32:30,043 --> 00:32:33,869
Let's see the ends of the world together

463
00:32:33,957 --> 00:32:38,304
Together, we can go and fly

464
00:32:38,304 --> 00:32:41,999
er, we can go and